Think of it this way: what’s happening when we observe a particle being shot towards a barrier only for it to remain a particle on impact means a choice has been made due to observation. That singular choice creates a singular point on the barrier. When a particle is shot towards a barrier and not observed, it acts like a wave, which is a physical reflection of the many places a particle could be on the barrier. No observation was made, meaning no choices were made regarding the particle or its conclusion. A wave looks like a straight line, but really a wave only looks like a line when in reality it is many different singular points arranged in a way that looks like a line. A wave is many points, each with their own direction to move in away from the point of origin. The observed particle is like a single choice i make and then follow, where a wave is like a spiritual stochastic process where i haven’t made any one choice.

A spiritual stochastic process is one where when i imagine multiple outcomes to one problem, the solution that may have a positive result is often the choice i make that pushes me out of my comfort zone. For as long as i can remember in the time before my Awakening i put such a strong emphasis on my personal comfort and safety that i rarely if ever changed my station in life. Often i wound up causing myself more stress because i wanted so badly for there to be no stress. Life doesn’t work that way for me. i have to be able to “go with the flow,” to take situations as they are in my reality and deal with them as best as i’m able at any moment. Taking time to slow down and consider actions and responses benefits me greatly. It’s something i struggle with (thanks ADHD) but all i can do is try to remain as mindful:present as possible.

